1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,178
Mort the Teenage Dirtbag: he's brought masks of every Final Girl killer to the

2
00:00:04,178 --> 00:00:06,167
convention, and he could be any of them.

3
00:00:06,387 --> 00:00:08,243
Here's how he plays: it's a whodunit.

4
00:00:09,067 --> 00:00:11,415
Put the Basic Finale card on the Killer board.

5
00:00:11,415 --> 00:00:14,528
It gives the Killer Action until the real Finale is revealed.

6
00:00:14,748 --> 00:00:17,979
Add the Interrogate and Coerce Action cards to the Tableau.

7
00:00:17,979 --> 00:00:22,523
Lay the ten Suspect cards in a row above the board, attributes side up, and put the

8
00:00:22,523 --> 00:00:24,604
ten Suspect tokens in the Suspect bag.

9
00:00:25,433 --> 00:00:29,723
Mort doesn't start on the board. After placing the Victims and yourself, place the

10
00:00:29,723 --> 00:00:33,647
ten Suspect miniatures at random on empty spaces, with nobody else in them.

11
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:38,135
If you run out of empty spaces, put the rest in the spaces farthest from you that

12
00:00:38,135 --> 00:00:40,032
have Victims, one Suspect per space.

13
00:00:40,252 --> 00:00:44,560
Then pick a Clue card at random and put it beside the board with the Clue Viewer and

14
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:48,303
the five Reminder tokens face down. That card decides who Mort really is.

15
00:00:48,303 --> 00:00:52,406
Put the Horror Track token on the Killer board, and don't open the Finale Secret

16
00:00:52,406 --> 00:00:53,585
Envelope until told to.

17
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:57,828
The ten Suspects are each dressed as a different Final Girl villain.

18
00:00:57,828 --> 00:01:00,097
They're not the Killer, an Enemy or a Victim:

19
00:01:00,097 --> 00:01:02,315
they're never targeted and can't be damaged.

20
00:01:02,535 --> 00:01:04,686
Each Suspect card lists seven attributes:

21
00:01:04,686 --> 00:01:08,726
series of origin, height, favourite board game style, favourite horror genre,

22
00:01:08,726 --> 00:01:12,241
favourite villain, favourite Van Ryder game, and mask or facepaint.

23
00:01:12,241 --> 00:01:13,500
Those are your evidence.

24
00:01:14,333 --> 00:01:18,790
Two Action cards do your detective work. Interrogate can only be resolved in a space

25
00:01:18,790 --> 00:01:22,292
with a Suspect. A success panics the Suspect and reveals one Clue.

26
00:01:22,292 --> 00:01:26,643
With no successes the Suspect still panics, and the card goes back into your hand.

27
00:01:26,863 --> 00:01:30,950
Coerce works on Informants instead: it can only be resolved in a space with an

28
00:01:30,950 --> 00:01:35,247
Informant, and after a successful Coerce you remove that Informant from the board.

29
00:01:36,067 --> 00:01:40,373
To reveal a Clue, flip one of the face-down Reminder tokens, numbered one to five,

30
00:01:40,373 --> 00:01:43,471
and use the Clue Viewer to read that Clue on the Clue card.

31
00:01:43,471 --> 00:01:45,624
It names an attribute Mort does not have.

32
00:01:45,844 --> 00:01:49,926
Discard every Suspect card with that attribute, and swap each discarded Suspect's

33
00:01:49,926 --> 00:01:52,295
miniature on the board for an Informant meeple.

34
00:01:52,295 --> 00:01:55,721
Keep the Reminder token face up so you know which Clues you've seen.

35
00:01:55,941 --> 00:01:59,034
Every Clue eliminates at least one Suspect, often more.

36
00:01:59,034 --> 00:02:03,475
For example, Josie reads Clue two: Mort's favourite genre is not comedy horror.

37
00:02:03,475 --> 00:02:07,355
The H.U.N.T.E.R. and Baghead both love comedy horror, so they're out.

38
00:02:08,167 --> 00:02:11,431
Informants count as Victims for everything, with three exceptions.

39
00:02:11,651 --> 00:02:16,066
When you save an Informant, after your Final Girl reward you also lower Horror once.

40
00:02:16,066 --> 00:02:19,693
If one is killed, after raising Bloodlust you must raise Horror once.

41
00:02:19,913 --> 00:02:23,642
And when the Active Killer targets by nearest or farthest and there's a tie,

42
00:02:23,642 --> 00:02:25,801
Informants are chosen before normal Victims.

43
00:02:26,633 --> 00:02:29,574
Mort could be impersonating anyone, if only for a moment.

44
00:02:29,574 --> 00:02:32,927
When you see the Suspect icon, draw a token from the Suspect bag.

45
00:02:32,927 --> 00:02:37,105
That Suspect becomes the Active Killer for the Killer Action, then the token goes

46
00:02:37,105 --> 00:02:39,220
back in the bag, so they could act again.

47
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:43,645
Any Location card that makes the Killer act also draws a token, and that Suspect

48
00:02:43,645 --> 00:02:46,011
resolves all the Killer effects on that card.

49
00:02:46,231 --> 00:02:50,526
If you draw a Suspect who's already been cleared, nothing happens and that token is

50
00:02:50,526 --> 00:02:54,615
discarded instead of going back. Clearing Suspects early really slows him down.

51
00:02:55,433 --> 00:02:59,197
When Bloodlust reaches the top of its track, move the Horror Track token from the

52
00:02:59,197 --> 00:03:02,310
Killer board onto the end of the Horror track on your Player board.

53
00:03:02,310 --> 00:03:05,097
From then on, if Horror would go past the maximum, you lose.

54
00:03:05,317 --> 00:03:08,816
And until Mort is revealed, Victims don't panic in the Panic phase.

55
00:03:09,633 --> 00:03:12,606
When all five Clues are revealed, only one Suspect is left.

56
00:03:12,606 --> 00:03:14,874
Flip the Clue card and check with the Viewer:

57
00:03:14,874 --> 00:03:15,479
that's Mort.

58
00:03:15,699 --> 00:03:18,770
Discard any Minor Dark Powers and the rest of the Terror deck.

59
00:03:18,770 --> 00:03:22,931
Swap that Suspect's miniature for Mort's, and remove every Informant from the board.

60
00:03:23,151 --> 00:03:27,315
Flip that Suspect's card: it's his Finale, and it replaces the Basic Finale.

61
00:03:27,315 --> 00:03:31,698
Reveal the Dark Power if it isn't out yet, and give Mort the health on the card,

62
00:03:31,698 --> 00:03:35,588
including a Final Health token. Josie's Mort was Hans, with ten health.

63
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:40,484
If the Terror deck runs out before you've found all five Clues, the Finale comes

64
00:03:40,484 --> 00:03:44,721
anyway. Flip the Clue card to reveal him, put Mort's miniature in place, and remove

65
00:03:44,721 --> 00:03:46,661
all the other Suspects and Informants.

66
00:03:46,881 --> 00:03:51,303
He takes the health on his card, and each Finale gets a bonus for every unrevealed

67
00:03:51,303 --> 00:03:54,538
Clue. Put a Reminder token on the card to remember how many.

68
00:03:54,538 --> 00:03:58,636
Mort as Hans, for example, adds two to his Attack Value per unrevealed Clue.

69
00:03:59,467 --> 00:04:03,776
Anonymous Terror: each unrevealed Clue counts as two when the Finale is revealed.

70
00:04:03,996 --> 00:04:08,122
The Epic Snitches Get Stitches: after Suspects become Informants, roll a die;

71
00:04:08,122 --> 00:04:10,908
on one to four, one of the new Informants is killed.

72
00:04:11,128 --> 00:04:15,291
Relentless Paranoia stops saving Informants lowering Horror, and Toxic Whispers

73
00:04:15,291 --> 00:04:18,189
makes you roll one fewer die on Interrogate and Coerce.

74
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:23,395
His Minor Dark Powers, like Quick Slash, which costs you a health per Clue, can be

75
00:04:23,395 --> 00:04:27,523
discarded early: each two-star success on Interrogate or Coerce discards one.

76
00:04:27,523 --> 00:04:29,667
They all go when the Finale is revealed.

77
00:04:29,887 --> 00:04:33,856
If a Location's Minor Dark Power has spaces for Health markers, don't add any:

78
00:04:33,856 --> 00:04:36,095
Mort can't be attacked while he's disguised.

79
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:41,167
A few tips. Clear Suspects early: a cleared Suspect's Killer actions do nothing.

80
00:04:41,387 --> 00:04:45,773
Aim to reveal all five Clues before the Terror deck runs out, or his Finale gets

81
00:04:45,773 --> 00:04:46,485
much nastier.

82
00:04:46,705 --> 00:04:49,977
He raises Horror a lot, so keep Horror-reducing cards coming.

83
00:04:49,977 --> 00:04:52,551
Players win about two games in three. Good luck.

